Ahh—good catch. This is one of those confusing SharePoint + Power Apps quirks 👍


---

🎯 WHAT’S REALLY HAPPENING

In SharePoint:

Question No → (renamed column)
Actual internal name = Title

👉 Even if you renamed it to “Question No”, Power Apps often still uses:

Title


---

✅ WHY YOUR TEST BEHAVES LIKE THIS

❌ This errors:

LookUp('SE Question List', 'Question No' = "M1R")

Because:

Power Apps does NOT recognize the display name

Or it expects special syntax for renamed columns



---

✅ This works:

LookUp('SE Question List', Title = "M1R")

Because:

Title is the internal column name



---

🔥 FINAL DECISION (IMPORTANT)

👉 Use Title for your Question No


---

✅ FIX YOUR MAIN CODE

Replace:

'Question No' = "M1R"

👉 WITH:

Title = "M1R"


---

🧠 ALSO FIX THIS PART (SECOND ISSUE)

Your column:

Section In-charge (Lookup)

Sometimes Power Apps reads it as:

'Section In-charge'

BUT the .Value part depends on the lookup configuration.


