> ❌ “Incompatible types for comparison… Error, Text”




---

🎯 ROOT CAUSE

This line is the problem:

Title = "M1R"

👉 In your SE Question List, you changed:

❌ Title → no longer used as Question No

✅ Question No is now your identifier


So Power Apps is trying to compare:

Title (empty / different type)

"M1R" (Text)


➡️ Result: Type mismatch error


---

✅ FIX 1: USE CORRECT COLUMN (VERY IMPORTANT)

Replace:

Title = "M1R"

👉 WITH:

'Question No' = "M1R"


---

🎯 ROOT CAUSE #2 (SECOND ISSUE)

This part can also break:

'Section Incharge'.Value = Dropdown_Section.Selected.Title

Your actual column name is:

Section In-charge (Lookup)

👉 Power Apps is very strict with names


---

✅ FIX 2: CORRECT LOOKUP COLUMN NAME

Replace:

'Section Incharge'.Value

👉 WITH:

'Section In-charge'.Value


